{#
  Email capture. Renders nothing until `formAction` is set in _data/newsletter.json,
  so we can never ship a form that quietly drops addresses on the floor.

  The form posts straight to the email provider — no JavaScript, and no backend of
  ours in the path. `formAction` holds the whole provider URL rather than just an
  account name, so swapping providers is a one-line data change, not a template edit.

  Include this at most once per page: the ids below have to stay unique.

  Consent, in two layers:
  1. The checkbox is unchecked by default and `required`, so the browser refuses to
     submit without it. It deliberately carries no `name` attribute — it must not be
     sent to the provider, which rejects unrecognised fields or bills them as
     metadata. Its only job is to gate submission here.
  2. The provider emails a confirmation link and holds the address inactive until
     the reader clicks it. That double opt-in is the real consent record.
#}
{% if newsletter.formAction %}
  <section class="subscribe" aria-labelledby="subscribe-heading">
    <h2 id="subscribe-heading">{{ newsletter.heading }}</h2>
    <p>{{ newsletter.pitch }}</p>

    <form class="subscribe-form" action="{{ newsletter.formAction }}" method="post">
      <div class="subscribe-row">
        <label for="subscribe-email">Email address</label>
        <input
          type="email"
          name="email"
          id="subscribe-email"
          autocomplete="email"
          spellcheck="false"
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          required
        />
      </div>

      <div class="subscribe-consent">
        <input type="checkbox" id="subscribe-consent" required />
        <label for="subscribe-consent">{{ newsletter.consent }}</label>
      </div>

      <input type="hidden" name="embed" value="1" />
      <button type="submit">{{ newsletter.buttonLabel }}</button>

      <p class="meta">
        We use your address to send you these emails and nothing else. Every email has
        a one-click unsubscribe link.
        <a href="/privacy/">How we handle your email</a>.
      </p>
    </form>
  </section>
{% endif %}
